# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two PUBLIC values. Both end up in the browser bundle, and that is fine:
# there are no accounts, and Row Level Security is what enforces the rules
# (see contracts/storage-api.md). A publishable key in the bundle is expected,
# not a leak.
#
# Get both from Supabase: Project Settings -> API.
#   URL  looks like https://abcdefghijkl.supabase.co
#   KEY  is the one labelled "publishable" (sb_publishable_...), or on older
#        projects "anon public".
#
# Two failure modes this file used to cause:
#   - Leaving a placeholder -> "TypeError: Failed to fetch", which names neither
#     the cause nor the fix.
#   - Pasting the SECRET key here -> "Forbidden use of secret API key in
#     browser", after the key has already shipped publicly.
# src/state/config.ts now catches both before the client is built, but do not
# rely on that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://REPLACE-ME.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=REPLACE-ME

# Both values must ALSO be set as GitHub repository secrets, under the same
# names. The deploy workflow builds with them, and the keep-alive workflow
# (.github/workflows/keepalive.yml) uses them to stop the free Supabase project
# pausing after 7 days of inactivity - see docs/adr/0007.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The SECRET value. Local migrations only. NEVER give it a VITE_ prefix and
# NEVER put it in VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY or in a repository secret used by the
# deploy workflow: every VITE_ variable is inlined into the published bundle,
# and this key bypasses every Row Level Security rule, including the one-run
# rule (FR-017/FR-018). If it ever reaches a browser, rotate it in Supabase
# immediately - the value, once published, is public forever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=only-for-local-migrations

# Organizer URL secret. Kept out of the player bundle; see FR-006.
# This is secrecy, not authentication - anyone holding it has organizer powers.
